      ],
      "start": 1066.92,
      "end": 1071.8
    },
    {
      "en": "Today, we've invited Dr. Caspar Melville, lecturer from the University of London.",
      "asr_range": [
        1765,
        1777
      ],
      "start": 1072.36,
      "end": 1077.88
    },
    {
      "en": "Dr. Melville started out as a music journalist for a black music magazine called Blues and Soul.",
      "asr_range": [
        1777,
        1794
      ],
      "start": 1078.73,
      "end": 1085.61
    },
    {
      "en": "In nineteen ninety-two, he moved to San Francisco and founded a jazz magazine named On the One, with some friends.",
      "asr_range": [
        1794,
        1815
      ],
      "start": 1085.85,
      "end": 1094.75
    },
    {
      "en": "They did a really good job, though there was not a lot of money in it.",
      "asr_range": [
        1815,
        1831
      ],
      "start": 1094.99,
      "end": 1099.39
    },
    {
      "en": "In nineteen ninety-seven, he moved back to London and started teaching, and made the decision to find another way to write about music.",
      "asr_range": [
        1831,
        1855
      ],
      "start": 1099.95,
      "end": 1108.11
    },
    {
      "en": "He grew up in London.",
      "asr_range": [
        1855,
        1860
      ],
      "start": 1108.86,
      "end": 1110.62
    },
    {
      "en": "He feels that the music in London clubs has formed him, but unfortunately it has been seriously undervalued by the academic world.",
      "asr_range": [
        1860,
        1882
      ],
      "start": 1110.86,
      "end": 1119.18
    },
    {
      "en": "In black music studies, jazz has received great attention, but dance music has been largely ignored.",
